/*
 * Declares the ArrayValue class.
 *
 * ArrayValue represents a literal array constructed from a list of inner
 * literal or non-literal values. It corresponds to array literals written in
 * source code(e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) or generated during semantic lowering.
 *
 * An ArrayValue:
 *   - stores the list of element values,
 *   - computes its throwers from the union of its elements’ throwers,
 *   - is considered a full literal only if all its elements are full literals,
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::literal::array
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/literal/array.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
